# Linear governance — iPix

## Plain English (why this rule exists)

When Maya plans Spring Campaign in Command Center, Linear must show who owns what and what is Done — not a stale markdown tracker. Agents that trust repo summaries invent wrong blockers and mark AI chat “fixed” when `/info` still 403s. This rule forces **live Linear** reads, safe writes, and evidence-backed Done.

**Real-world iPix:** Operator signs in → brand/org resolves → CopilotKit `/info` 200 → Production Planner. Governance mistakes (wrong project, fake Done, cycle spam) hide the real failure (e.g. missing `org_members` on **IPI-935**).

## Scope

Stable **how** to use Linear. Never treat this file as SSOT for dates, statuses, cycle windows, or ownership — those live in **live Linear**.

Companions: `.claude/skills/linear/` · `task-naming.mdc` · `docs/process/templates/task-execution-prompt.md` · detail: `references/governance-detail.md` (load on demand).

## Source of truth

| Information | Authority |
|-------------|-----------|
| Status, project, milestone, cycle, priority, owner | Live Linear |
| Code | `origin/main` + open PR / worktree |
| Production behavior | Browser / production probe |
| Requirements / AC | Canonical issue / `docs/linear/issues/` |
| Repo trackers / `live-workspace-state.md` | Summary only — may be stale |

Conflict → **report**, do not silently overwrite.

## Access & safety

| Prefer | Fallback |
|--------|----------|
| Linear MCP (`plugin-linear-linear`) | GraphQL + `LINEAR_API_KEY` only when MCP cannot set a field |

Never print secrets. Never delete projects/issues unless asked. Bulk/destructive → propose first, apply after approval. Discover MCP tools each session. GraphQL only after inspect + listed entities + approval for bulk.

## Naming & one concern

- Titles / first mention: **`IPI-NNN · SPEC — Plain English`** (`task-naming.mdc`)
- Team: **iPix1** (`IPI`)
- One independently testable outcome per issue/PR
- Never mix unrelated docs + production code (AGENTS.md #1)

## Ownership (short)

Attach issues to the project that **owns delivery**. Resolve names via live Linear — do not invent. Detail + examples → skill `governance-detail.md`.

## Status & Done

| State | When |
|-------|------|
| Backlog | Unscheduled |
| Todo | Ready to start |
| In Progress | Actively executing |
| Done | ACs met + evidence (`origin/main`, tests, **browser**) — never status-copy alone |
| Duplicate | `duplicateOf` set |
| Canceled | Explicitly abandoned |

Reopen Done only with approval (unless the task authorizes correction). Record the unmet AC first.

## Cycles & dependencies (short)

- Cycle = work expected to **start or progress** in-window; owned; capacity-backed; not every important ticket
- Relations: `blocks` / `blockedBy` / `relatedTo` / `duplicateOf` — not prose-only depends-on
- Scan for open dependency cycles; keep valid Done history edges
- Detail, HOLD DNS, milestone patterns → `governance-detail.md`

## Read → mutate → verify

**Read-only:** discover MCP → list filtered issues/project/cycles → spot-check → dependency scan → compare to `origin/main` (label STALE) → PASS / NEEDS FIXES; mutate only when asked.

**Mutate:** confirm approval → change milestones/cycles/deps → cleanup noise → optional project update → re-read live → LINEAR FIX VERDICT.

## Issue create / rewrite checklist

- [ ] Dedupe by title/identifier
- [ ] Full title + team IPI
- [ ] Prepend `<task_execution>` from `docs/process/templates/task-execution-prompt.md` if missing (skip Dupes / noise / pure trackers unless asked)
- [ ] Correct project + milestone (active delivery) + optional cycle
- [ ] Hard `blockedBy` / `blocks` when needed
- [ ] Labels that match track

Humans: IPI team default template — `docs/process/templates/LINEAR-DEFAULT-INSTALL.md`.

Do **not** paste the full Staff XML into this alwaysApply rule.

## AI task execution (pointer)

For every **executable** IPI issue, follow the SSOT prompt (research → reuse → implement → test → browser → update Linear → DoD). Do not reload the full XML here.

```text
1 Explain simply · 2 Real iPix workflow · 3 Research official docs + repo
4 Audit existing code · 5 Reuse before build · 6 Plan · 7 Implement
8 Tests · 9 Browser (Playwright / Chrome MCP) · 10 Docs · 11 Linear · 12 DoD
```

Reuse search before code: repo helpers, APIs, Supabase, Mastra, CopilotKit, Cloudflare, MCP, Edge Functions, agents, workflows, dashboards.

**Done requires:** ACs · tests · browser (or honest N/A) · docs · Linear updated · no duplicate impl · fail-closed auth preserved · rollback considered when risky.

PR body (when shipping code): problem · solution · files · tests · risks · rollback · evidence — plus `pr-description.mdc` plain-English sections.

## Anti-patterns

| ❌ Don’t | ✅ Do |
|---------|--------|
| Trust markdown dates/examples | Live Linear |
| Bare `IPI-249` in user text | Full **IPI-249 · SPEC — …** |
| Mark Done from sibling merge | Evidence for **this** issue |
| Cycle-stuff every ticket | Capacity-backed only |
| Milestone to inflate % | Outcome-bearing delivery |
| Weaken fail-closed auth for green `/info` | Fix data/env (e.g. `org_members`) |
| Full Staff XML in alwaysApply | Point to `task-execution-prompt.md` |

